                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "570ad3a1-f6fb-385c-8cd3-9f60738ddee7",
                                        "entry_id": "2d30ff0f-ea55-388e-a6c7-f0cf97768cc0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A toroidal bread roll that is boiled before it is baked."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c647775a-6be9-3ec0-a032-b271629fe73c",
                                        "entry_id": "2d30ff0f-ea55-388e-a6c7-f0cf97768cc0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A score of 6-0 in a set (after the shape of a bagel, which looks like a zero)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7625e1bc-a769-40c7-a045-71fcd2e3cd37",
                                                "sense_id": "c647775a-6be9-3ec0-a032-b271629fe73c",
                                                "text": "The Scot, who had been close to a two-set deficit in his semi-final against David Ferrer, avoided the dreaded bagel by seeing off a set point at 5-0 down before finally breaking the Djokovic serve to love as he began to go for his shots with the set seemingly gone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "11411c39-98ea-331f-b270-7293ee7c4d4a",
                                        "entry_id": "2d30ff0f-ea55-388e-a6c7-f0cf97768cc0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An overly materialistic and selfish young Jewish man."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "South-Africa",
                                            "ethnic",
                                            "slang",
                                            "slur"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bagel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2648836-783c-390c-be04-8ae06fddb4f5",
                                        "entry_id": "60ce1e21-be37-3d6f-99c2-0f6c8eb3ba4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To achieve a score of 6–0 (as the winner) in a tennis set."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8812a610-db83-3897-adce-11eb475134d5",
                                        "entry_id": "60ce1e21-be37-3d6f-99c2-0f6c8eb3ba4b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To hold an opponent to a score of zero."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bagel",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fe4c18e4-652a-349c-bb08-5c55304a3a9c",
                                        "entry_id": "80662de8-e72c-3b1b-aa3c-e59343c4a3fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative form of bagle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4cecac24-076e-4e11-a728-10ad798841b3",
                                                "sense_id": "fe4c18e4-652a-349c-bb08-5c55304a3a9c",
                                                "text": "“He’s so adorable, Aaron. Part beagle, part basset hound.” “A bagel. Very appropriate.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "574c0ae7-c5f8-45a4-8abf-9668756e235c",
                                                "sense_id": "fe4c18e4-652a-349c-bb08-5c55304a3a9c",
                                                "text": "In October, Allan and Rebecca began to care for Marty’s dog Phil more often and adopted the “bagel” (basset and beagle mix breed) when the time came."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4115e4a-9fe6-4328-8c3d-aed7e84b1f21",
                                                "sense_id": "fe4c18e4-652a-349c-bb08-5c55304a3a9c",
                                                "text": "The Bagel isn’t necessarily a popular dog, but they seem to appear often enough to be worth mentioning."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c225a867-a0f7-44b9-8c85-2c13a96c0e3e",
                                                "sense_id": "fe4c18e4-652a-349c-bb08-5c55304a3a9c",
                                                "text": "The Bagel is a cross between the Beagle and the Basset Hound. Though not as popular as some of the more well-established mixes, the short-coated Bagel has the loving personality one would expect from two Hounds, plus the potential for some stubbornness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7772217c-1b2c-4454-9501-1b7b01b70ede",
                                                "sense_id": "fe4c18e4-652a-349c-bb08-5c55304a3a9c",
                                                "text": "Linus was half basset and half beagle hound, thus a bagel."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "77542374-e7a6-4733-aba7-ea7f912fa748",
                        "source_entry_id": "67ae172f-e70d-3aa9-bc31-8679337c2d97",
